error[NK1257]: An `i64` is copied at a read, so a parameter can't be a `ref i64`.
  --> tests/grammar_ref_on_a_word_rule_value_is_refused.nika:7:12
   |
 7 | 	rule Item(n: ref i64) -> i64 = "x" -> { 1 }
   |            ^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: A number, a `bool`, a `scalar` and an enum whose variants hold nothing are copied at a read (ADR-279 D8): the copy is never dearer than a pointer, so `ref` on one says nothing. Only an `extern "C"` declaration writes it, as the pointer C expects.
   = help: Write `i64` without `ref`; a parameter the function changes is `mut name: i64`.
1 type error
